
# Supabase Configuration - TEMPLATE (Replace with your project values)
# These are the only environment variables that should be exposed to the client
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-id.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.your-anon-key-here

# CRITICAL HIPAA COMPLIANCE NOTES:
# 1. NEVER commit real .env files to Git - they contain production credentials
# 2. DO NOT add any sensitive keys that start with VITE_ as they will be exposed to the client
# 3. Server-side secrets like ENCRYPTION_SECRET should ONLY be configured in Supabase Edge Functions secrets
# 4. NEVER expose private keys, service role keys, or encryption secrets to the client

# Production Deployment Checklist:
# 1. Set these environment variables in your Vercel project settings (NOT in code)
# 2. Execute Business Associate Agreements (BAAs) with Supabase and Vercel
# 3. Configure Supabase Auth redirect URLs in your Supabase dashboard
# 4. Enable RLS policies on all tables with proper patient data protection
# 5. Review and test all security policies before deployment
# 6. Set up automated backup and disaster recovery procedures
# 7. Configure audit logging for all PHI access
# 8. Implement session timeout policies (15 minutes for PHI access)

# To get your actual values:
# 1. Go to https://supabase.com/dashboard
# 2. Create a new project or select existing project
# 3. Go to Settings > API
# 4. Copy Project URL and anon/public key
# 5. Paste them in your local .env file (which should NEVER be committed)
